<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-8oxsb: a partial index on nexus.memory (tenant_id, project, timestamp DESC, id DESC)
    WHERE quarantined_at IS NULL, for the bounded /v1/memory/list read.

    WHY. Since nexus-xn9ut a bounded list (MemoryRepository.listEntries with a limit) runs two
    queries: the newest N live rows of a project, ORDER BY timestamp DESC, id DESC, and
    countEntries, a count(*) of the same rows for the "N more" line. The list was never the cost:
    the planner already walks idx_memory_tenant_timestamp with an incremental sort. The count
    was, a sequential scan of the table on every bounded read. Measured on PG17.5 with the live
    store's shape (5,857 rows, ~5.4 KB content, the nexus project 65% of rows), as a non-superuser
    under FORCE RLS (critique T2 nexus/critique-nexus-8oxsb-e84984b1c):
      - count:  6.1 ms -> 0.87 ms (generic plan 1.6 -> 0.78 ms), index-only scan
      - list:   0.14 ms -> 0.06 ms
    A few ms per namespace a hook renders. A full (non-partial) index of the same columns leaves
    the count a seq scan, because quarantined_at is only in the heap; the predicate is what lets
    the count stay in the index. Every live read path filters quarantined_at IS NULL
    (MemoryRepository.NOT_QUARANTINED), so the index covers exactly the rows those reads return.

    BUILD WINDOW (the memory-004 precedent): plain CREATE INDEX, not CONCURRENTLY, which a
    Liquibase changeset's transaction does not allow. nexus.memory measured 5,854 rows / 71 MB on
    the live store (RDR-207 § Context); the build holds a SHARE lock (reads continue, writes wait)
    for the time it takes to index those rows.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="memory-005-1" author="nexus-8oxsb">
        <comment>
            Partial index on nexus.memory (tenant_id, project, timestamp DESC, id DESC) WHERE
            quarantined_at IS NULL for the bounded list and its count. Additive: no row changes.
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
CREATE INDEX idx_memory_live_tenant_project_ts
    ON nexus.memory (tenant_id, project, timestamp DESC, id DESC)
    WHERE quarantined_at IS NULL;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_memory_live_tenant_project_ts;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
